  "cli_result_text": "Submitted the full impact surface for the JSON\u2192`RealmExport` migration:\n\n**Schema/migration anchor**\n- `zerver/models/realm_audit_logs.py` \u2014 current tracking mechanism (`RealmAuditLog.extra_data` JSONField with `AuditLogEventType.REALM_EXPORTED = 206`); this is what the new `RealmExport` table replaces and what the backfill migration will read from\n- `zerver/migrations/0247_realmauditlog_event_type_to_int.py` \u2014 precedent for how the event-type/int mapping was introduced, useful pattern for the new migration\n\n**Direct references**\n- `zerver/models/__init__.py` \u2014 model registration point (new `RealmExport` import needs to land here)\n- `zerver/actions/realm_export.py` \u2014 actions layer: `notify_realm_export`, `do_delete_realm_export`\n- `zerver/views/realm_export.py` \u2014 views serving `/json/export/realm` (create/list/delete) and export consents\n- `zerver/models/realms.py` \u2014 `EXPORT_PUBLIC`/`EXPORT_FULL_*` constants referenced throughout\n\n**Indirect references (the \"tentacles\")**\n- `zerver/worker/deferred_work.py` \u2014 background worker's `realm_export` event handler that writes `started_timestamp`/`failed_timestamp`/`export_path` into `extra_data`\n- `zerver/lib/export.py` \u2014 core export logic: `do_export_realm`, `export_realm_wrapper`, `get_realm_exports_serialized` (the JSON-shape serializer that becomes the model's `to_dict`)\n- `zerver/lib/import_realm.py` \u2014 writes `REALM_EXPORTED` audit rows during import\n- `zerver/management/commands/export.py` \u2014 CLI export command, creates its own `RealmAuditLog` row\n- `zerver/tests/test_management_commands.py` \u2014 `TestExport` class covering the CLI path\n\n**Test coverage**\n- `zerver/tests/test_realm_export.py` \u2014 dedicated export endpoint tests (S3 + local uploads, rate limiting, failure/retry, deletion)\n- `zerver/tests/test_import_export.py` \u2014 round-trip export/import tests that create `REALM_EXPORTED` audit entries\n- `zerver/tests/test_events.py` \u2014 event-schema test asserting the `realm_export` event shape\n- `web/tests/lib/events.js` \u2014 frontend event fixture mirroring the same shape\n\n**Frontend/API surface (would need updating if the serialized shape changes)**\n- `web/src/settings_exports.ts` \u2014 TypeScript consumer of `export_url`/`failed_timestamp`/`deleted_timestamp`\n- `web/templates/settings/admin_export_list.hbs` \u2014 export list template\n- `zerver/openapi/zulip.yaml` \u2014 `RealmExport` API schema definition\n- `tools/linter_lib/custom_check.py` \u2014 has a special-case lint rule referencing `zerver/management/commands/export.py`\n\nNote: `zerver/migrations/0595_add_realmexport_table_and_backfill.py` does not exist in this repo snapshot \u2014 there is no `RealmExport` model anywhere in the codebase yet. Current tracking is entirely `RealmAuditLog.extra_data` (a JSONField column), not a JSON file on disk as described. The file list above is everything that touches the *existing* tracking mechanism and would need to be read/updated when introducing the new model and migration.",
